{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak unto Aaron your brother, that he come not at all times into the holy place.</b> 'And let him not die' — in the manner that his sons died. Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, gave a parable: To what may the thing be likened? To a physician who entered to see a sick man and said to him, 'Do not eat cold food and do not sleep on damp ground.' Another came after him and said to him, 'Do not eat cold food and do not sleep on damp ground, lest you die in the manner that so-and-so died.' This one spurred him on more than the first." "<b>For in the cloud I will appear upon the cover.</b> Scripture did not say ״כי אראה בענן על הכפורת״ — 'for I will appear in the cloud upon the cover' — for had it said so, it would be implied that the appearing would be in the cloud, and if so what superior distinction would the High Priest have over all the rest of Israel? For all Israel would see the Glory in the cloud, as it is written (Exodus 16:10) ״והנה כבוד ה׳ נראה בענן״ — 'and behold, the glory of YHWH appeared in the cloud' — to all the children of Israel, and furthermore it is written (Exodus 33:10) ״וראה כל העם את עמוד הענן״ — 'and all the people saw the pillar of cloud.' But now, when it says ״כי בענן אראה על הכפורת״ — 'for in the cloud I will appear upon the cover' — it explains that after he comes there in the cloud, the Glory would slip away from the cloud and become visible upon the cover, and because of this it attached the appearing to the cover. And so the way of the Glory all the rest of the days of the year was to appear there upon the cover, and the High Priest was not permitted to enter there all the rest of the days of the year but only on the Day of Atonement. Therefore on the Day of Atonement he needed the incense, so that there would be a covering for the eyes and his eyes would not feed upon the radiance of the Glory. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: ״כי בענן אראה על הכפורת״ — 'in the cloud of the incense I will appear upon the cover'; and from here that he needed to make a cloud of incense within the inner sanctuary, not that he should prepare it outside and bring it in, according to the opinion of the Sadducees. And so Scripture proves in the passage, for it says (Leviticus 16:13) ״וכסה ענן הקטורת את הכפרת אשר על העדות ולא ימות״ — 'and the cloud of the incense shall cover the cover that is upon the testimony, that he die not.' Therefore they established in the Gemara that these two verses — one is for punishment and one is for warning: ״כי בענן אראה״ is for the warning, and ״וכסה ענן הקטורת״ is for the punishment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:50.456511158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}